===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|vessel for holding or serving food}} A [[vessel]] such as a [[plate]] for holding or serving food, often flat with a depressed region in the middle.
#: {{syn|en|plate}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Judges|v|25|text=She brought forth butter in a lordly '''dish'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|contents of the vessel; a dishful}} The contents of such a vessel.
#: {{syn|en|dishful|plate|plateful}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''dish''' of stew}}
# {{senseid|en|any particular type of prepared food}} {{lb|en|metonym}} A specific type of prepared food.
#: {{ux|en|a vegetable '''dish'''}}
#: {{ux|en|this '''dish''' is filling and easily made}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Julius Caesar|II|i|passage=Let's carve him a '''dish''' fit for the gods}}
# {{senseid|en|in the plural, dirty dishes needing cleaning}} {{lb|en|in the plural}} [[tableware|Tableware]] (including [[cutlery]], etc, as well as [[crockery]]) that is to be or is being washed after being used to prepare, serve and eat a meal.
#: {{ux|en|It's your turn to wash the '''dishes'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|antenna shaped like a plate or bowl}} {{lb|en|telecommunication}} A type of [[antenna]] with a similar shape to a plate or [[bowl]].
#: {{ux|en|satellite '''dish'''}}
#: {{ux|en|radar '''dish'''}}
# {{senseid|en|sexually attractive person}} {{lb|en|slang}} A sexually attractive person.
#: {{syn|en|babe|fox}}
#: {{ux|en|quite a '''dish'''}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1993|author=Westwood Studios|title=Lands of Lore: The Throne of Chaos|publisher=Virgin Games
|passage=Have you seen the new apothecary? I think her name is Sadie. What a '''dish'''!}}
# {{senseid|en|state or degree of concavity}} {{lb|en|dated}} The state of being [[concave]], like a dish, or the degree of such [[concavity]].<ref name=Webster>{{R:Webster 1913}}</ref>
#: {{ux|en|the '''dish''' of a wheel}}
# {{senseid|en|hollow place, low-lying area}} A hollow place, as in a field.<ref name=Webster />
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1980|title=Nebraskaland|text=As I topped the ridge I missed my first shot at a sharptail that flushed from a grassy '''dish'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1987|month=02|author=Brian Garfield|title=The Arizonans|publisher=Bantam|isbn=9780553262865
|text=He and Stratemeier raced across the flats and dropped into the canyon, climbed swiftly through it and came out at the topside trail , which went straight south through the timber until it dropped into a small grassy '''dish''' surrounded by rock peaks.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2006-09-14|author=Richard Holmes|author2=Martin Marix Evans|title=A Guide to Battles: Decisive Conflicts in History|publisher=OUP Oxford|isbn=9780191501173
|text=Daylight revealed that the so-called summit was near the edge of a shallow, stony '''dish''', which terminated abruptly in steep slopes, and actually offered poor fields of fire.}}
# {{senseid|en|home plate in baseball}} {{lb|en|baseball|slang}} The [[home plate]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2008|author=Paul Byrd|title=Free Byrd: The Power of a Liberated Life|page=4
|passage=He said, "I don't like your chances at the '''dish''' [home plate] tonight."}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2009|author=Loren Long; Phil Bildner|title=Magic in the Outfield|page=40
|passage=At the plate, Graham pounded the '''dish''' three times, just like Bubbles did whenever he was up, {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2014|author=Conor Kelley|title=The Catcher's Handbook|page=87
|passage=Also, if you end up getting to the baseball, your pitcher needs to be covering home plate, which pitchers occasionally forget to do. However, if the ball stays near the '''dish''' and you have a pitcher on the mound who isn't a space-case, you've got a good shot to get the runner out.}}
# {{senseid|en|trough for measuring ore}} {{lb|en|mining|archaic}} A [[trough]] in which [[ore]] is [[measure]]d.<ref name=Webster />
# {{senseid|en|mineral royalties or similar fees}} {{lb|en|mining|archaic}} That portion of the [[produce]] of a [[mine]] which is paid to the land owner or [[proprietor]].<ref name=Webster />
# {{senseid|en|gossip, as noun}} {{lb|en|slang|uncountable}} [[gossip|Gossip]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=24 Dec 89|volume=17|number=24|journal=Gay Community News|page=5|author=Abe Rybeck|title=Liberation Without Permission, Pleasure Without Apology|text=We've been a very lucky community: We've had GCN to collect our deep '''dish''' and write it up as political discourse. GCN is not just another clipboard of polite press releases. GCN is the sticky questions, the sweet moments, and the dirty stories that make up our lives.}}

